PACK|storage-backup-hygiene-2026-05-23|Storage and Backup Hygiene|Commands for finding backup bloat, moving ISO/image files to review folders, checking mounted backup drives, and running safer rsync backups.|1.0

ITEM|Find local ISO and VM images|find ~/Documents -type f \( -iname '*.iso' -o -iname '*.img' -o -iname '*.qcow2' -o -iname '*.vdi' -o -iname '*.vmdk' \) -printf '%s\t%p\n' | sort -nr | numfmt --field=1 --to=iec|Finds large image files under Documents.|Useful before backups to avoid repeated ISO/VM duplication.|linux,storage,backup,safe
ITEM|Move local ISO images to review folder|mkdir -p ~/Downloads/ISO && find ~/Documents -type f \( -iname '*.iso' -o -iname '*.img' -o -iname '*.qcow2' -o -iname '*.vdi' -o -iname '*.vmdk' \) -exec mv -v {} ~/Downloads/ISO/ \;|Moves disk images out of Documents into a review folder.|Review before deleting.|linux,storage,cleanup,caution
ITEM|Check mounted backup drives|lsblk -f && echo && df -h | grep -E 'Filesystem|/mnt|/data|/fastdata'|Shows block devices and mounted backup/storage filesystems.|Useful after power loss or before backup jobs.|linux,storage,diagnostics,safe
ITEM|Find backup drive image files|find /mnt/expansion /mnt/backup_main -type f \( -iname '*.iso' -o -iname '*.img' -o -iname '*.qcow2' -o -iname '*.vdi' -o -iname '*.vmdk' \) | wc -l|Counts remaining disk images on backup drives.|Useful after cleanup.|linux,backup,storage,safe
ITEM|Move backup drive images to Baxter Downloads|STAMP=$(date +%Y-%m-%d-%H%M%S); DEST="$HOME/Downloads/ISO-moved-from-backups-$STAMP"; mkdir -p "$DEST"; find /mnt/expansion /mnt/backup_main -type f \( -iname '*.iso' -o -iname '*.img' -o -iname '*.qcow2' -o -iname '*.vdi' -o -iname '*.vmdk' \) -exec mv -v {} "$DEST"/ \;|Moves ISO/image files from backup drives into a dated review folder.|Run on Baxter after verifying mount paths.|linux,backup,cleanup,caution
ITEM|Create dated backup folders on two drives|STAMP=$(date +%Y-%m-%d-%H%M%S); mkdir -p /mnt/expansion/lenovo-debian-Documents-$STAMP /mnt/backup_main/lenovo-debian-Documents-$STAMP|Creates dated backup targets on both backup drives.|Run on the backup server where drives are mounted.|linux,backup,organization,safe
ITEM|Rsync Documents excluding disk images|rsync -avh --progress --exclude='*.iso' --exclude='*.ISO' --exclude='*.img' --exclude='*.IMG' --exclude='*.qcow2' --exclude='*.vdi' --exclude='*.vmdk' ~/Documents/ user@host:/path/to/dated-backup/|Backs up Documents while excluding ISO/VM image files.|Edit destination before running.|linux,rsync,backup,safe
ITEM|Fix backup drive ownership|sudo chown -R "$USER:$USER" /mnt/expansion /mnt/backup_main|Sets backup drive ownership to current user.|Use only on personal/admin-controlled backup drives.|linux,permissions,backup,caution
ITEM|Set backup directory permissions|sudo chmod -R u+rwX,g+rwX,o-rwx /mnt/expansion /mnt/backup_main && sudo find /mnt/expansion /mnt/backup_main -type d -exec chmod g+s {} \;|Sets owner/group access and setgid directories.|Use on trusted personal backup drives.|linux,permissions,backup,caution
ITEM|Directory size summary|TARGET="$HOME/Documents"; du -h --max-depth=1 "$TARGET" | sort -h|Shows top-level directory sizes.|Change TARGET before running.|linux,storage,diagnostics,safe
ITEM|Find nested Documents folders|find ~/Documents -type d \( -name Documents -o -name 'Documents-*' \) -print|Helps detect accidental recursive backup folders.|Useful when backup trees start ballooning.|linux,backup,diagnostics,safe
